    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "The average of three numbers is $-56$. Two of the numbers are $20$ and $-10$. The third number is $x$. Write an equation for $x$ and solve it.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{20+(-10)+x}{3}=-56$, so $x=-178$.",
      "worked": "The average is the sum of the three numbers divided by $3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{20+(-10)+x}{3}&=-56\\\\10+x&=-168\\\\x&=-178\\end{align*}$$",
